{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790409963243,"sessionID":"ses_f23415950ffei6lPEGq2rMUxe4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_91aca7a52a484e56a39baaed","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the project structure in /workspace. Find all files, especially any related to \"SteerComponent\" (any file with \"steer\" in the name, case-insensitive). Also look for any debug-related files or overlay systems. Return the full file paths and directory structure.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f234100ceffecjZ3TnQn1LDvFM\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a complete report of the project structure and findings.\n\n---\n\n## Project Overview\n\nThis is a **Godot 4.2** project named **\"Buffer Steering Debug Vectors\"**, described as: *\"Record steering forces for visual debugging as described in Cashew OldDew's tutorial.\"* The main scene is `res://scenes/main.tscn`, and it uses the `gl_compatibility` renderer.\n\n---\n\n## Full Directory Tree\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   ├── filesystem_cache10\n│   │   ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│   │   └── project_metadata.cfg\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   ├── imported/\n│   │   ├── fishTile_078.png-4ff81e6b2fb335b54ebde3776fd0bc31.ctex\n│   │   └── fishTile_078.png-4ff81e6b2fb335b54ebde3776fd0bc31.md5\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n│   └── uid_cache.bin\n├── assets/\n│   └── sprites/\n│       ├── fishTile_078.png\n│       └── fishTile_078.png.import\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── fish.tscn\n│   ├── main.tscn\n│   └── steer_component.tscn\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── fish.gd\n│   ├── fish.gd.uid\n│   ├── steer_component.gd\n│   └── steer_component.gd.uid\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## Files Matching \"Steer\" (case-insensitive)\n\nThree files were found:\n\n| # | Absolute Path | Description |\n|---|---------------|-------------|\n| 1 | `/workspace/scenes/steer_component.tscn` | PackedScene for the SteerComponent node (type `Node2D`) |\n| 2 | `/workspace/scripts/steer_component.gd` | GDScript implementing the steering logic |\n| 3 | `/workspace/scripts/steer_component.gd.uid` | Godot's UID file for the script |\n\n---\n\n## Files Matching \"Debug\" or \"Overlay\"\n\n**No files** were found with `debug` or `overlay` in their filenames. However, the concept of debugging is central to the project:\n\n- `/workspace/project.godot` names the project **\"Buffer Steering Debug Vectors\"**.\n- `/workspace/task_config.json` contains the instruction: *\"Inside the SteerComponent script, capture the current velocity, scaled desired velocity, and steering force in a debug dictionary whenever debugging is enabled, and queue a redraw every frame so the overlay can update.\"*\n\nThis indicates debug/overlay functionality is **meant to be implemented inside** `steer_component.gd`, not in separate files.\n\n---\n\n## Key File Contents (Summary)\n\n### `/workspace/scripts/steer_component.gd`\nThe core script. Currently:\n- Has a `debug_enabled` boolean (`false` by default) and a `debug` Dictionary.\n- Implements a `steer()` function that calculates desired velocity, scaled desired velocity, and a steering adjustment based on mass.\n- Has empty stubs for `update_debug()`, `_process()`, and `_draw()`.\n- **Not yet capturing debug data or calling `queue_redraw()`** -- this is the task described in `task_config.json`.\n\n### `/workspace/scripts/fish.gd`\nThe fish character controller:\n- Extends `CharacterBody2D`.\n- References the `SteerComponent` child node via `$SteerComponent`.\n- In `_ready()`, sets `debug_enabled = true` on the SteerComponent if it has a `set` method.\n- In `_physics_process()`, gets the mouse position as a target, calls `steer_component.steer()`, rotates the sprite toward velocity, and calls `move_and_slide()`.\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/fish.tscn`\n- Instances the `Fish` scene (`CharacterBody2D`) with a sprite (using `fishTile_078.png`), a collision shape, and a child `SteerComponent` (instanced from `steer_component.tscn`).\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`\n- Minimal root scene containing just one `Fish` instance.\n\n### `/workspace/project.godot`\n- Project config; main scene is `scenes/main.tscn`, using GL Compatibility renderer.\n\n### `/workspace/task_config.json`\n- A task instruction JSON describing what needs to be implemented in the SteerComponent.\n\n---\n\n## Conclusion\n\nThe project is a small Godot 4.2 steering-behavior demo. There are **no existing debug-specific or overlay-specific files** -- the debug overlay system is the feature to be built inside the existing `steer_component.gd` script, per the task configuration. All project source files are concentrated in `/workspace/scenes/` and `/workspace/scripts/`.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f23415950ffei6lPEGq2rMUxe4","sessionId":"ses_f234100ceffecjZ3TnQn1LDvFM","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790409899828,"end":1790409963221}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_fed48b06-0bc8-4a77-b52a-0a74301883ef"}},"id":"prt_0dcbeff280013AzXmmzumcwDul","sessionID":"ses_f23415950ffei6lPEGq2rMUxe4","messageID":"msg_0dcbea898001sZyfeNwvBay6hO"}}
